# Shining Wind (PS2) — Reverse Engineering & Translation Project

Reverse engineering research and fan translation groundwork for **Shining Wind (PlayStation 2, 2006)** developed by Media.Vision and published by SEGA.

This repository documents the internal structure of the game, file formats, and extraction pipelines required to access dialogue, audio, and script data for translation and reinsertion.

---

## 📌 Project Goals

- Extract all in-game text (dialogue, UI, database entries)
- Map voice lines ↔ subtitles using internal IDs
- Reverse engineer proprietary Media.Vision formats
- Build tooling for translation reinsertion
- Prepare full fan translation pipeline

---

## 🗂 Disc Structure


CD/
├── SLPM_666.71 # Main PS2 ELF (MIPS executable)
├── MODULES.LST # Module list
├── MODULES.CIX # Memory index
├── modules/ # IOP drivers (CRI, PAD, etc.)
├── st.cvm # Main game data container
└── voice.cvm # Voice audio archive (.ADX)


---

## 📦 CVM Containers

The game uses **CVM archives (ISO-like containers)**.

- `st.cvm` → game assets (scripts, textures, data)
- `voice.cvm` → voice audio only (.ADX)

Extractable via **QuickBMS**.

---

## 🎤 voice.cvm

### Structure

Voice data is organized by scenario folders:

- `E01–E11` → main story events  
- `H01–H11` → heroine routes  
- `M00–M16` → main arc  
- `S00–S14` → side characters  

### Notes

- Contains only `.ADX` audio files
- No text/subtitles included
- Some entries are missing (e.g. S00 incomplete set)

### Key Insight

> Subtitle data is NOT in voice.cvm  
> It is stored in `st.cvm → PAC_TOWN##_01.RAX`

